=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::Operation

This operation resource represents operations that may have happened or are
happening on the cluster. All fields are output only.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The server-assigned ID for the operation.

=item * C<< $msg->zone() >> / C<< $msg->zone($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine
[zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the operation is taking place. This field is deprecated, use
location instead.

=item * C<< $msg->operation_type() >> / C<< $msg->operation_type($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1::Operation::Type>)

Output only. The operation type.

=item * C<< $msg->status() >> / C<< $msg->status($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1::Operation::Status>)

Output only. The current status of the operation.

=item * C<< $msg->detail() >> / C<< $msg->detail($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Detailed operation progress, if available.

=item * C<< $msg->status_message() >> / C<< $msg->status_message($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. If an error has occurred, a textual description of the error.
Deprecated. Use the field error instead.

=item * C<< $msg->self_link() >> / C<< $msg->self_link($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Server-defined URI for the operation. Example:
`https://container.googleapis.com/v1alpha1/projects/123/locations/us-central1/operations/operation-123`.

=item * C<< $msg->target_link() >> / C<< $msg->target_link($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Server-defined URI for the target of the operation. The format
of this is a URI to the resource being modified (such as a cluster, node
pool, or node). For node pool repairs, there may be multiple nodes being
repaired, but only one will be the target.

Examples:

-
##
`https://container.googleapis.com/v1/projects/123/locations/us-central1/clusters/my-cluster`

##
`https://container.googleapis.com/v1/projects/123/zones/us-central1-c/clusters/my-cluster/nodePools/my-np`

`https://container.googleapis.com/v1/projects/123/zones/us-central1-c/clusters/my-cluster/nodePools/my-np/node/my-node`

=item * C<< $msg->location() >> / C<< $msg->location($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine
[zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available)
or
[region](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available)
in which the cluster resides.

=item * C<< $msg->start_time() >> / C<< $msg->start_time($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The time the operation started, in
[RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.

=item * C<< $msg->end_time() >> / C<< $msg->end_time($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The time the operation completed, in
[RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.

=item * C<< $msg->progress() >> / C<< $msg->progress($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::OperationProgress>)

Output only. Progress information for an operation.

=item * C<< $msg->cluster_conditions() >> / C<< $msg->cluster_conditions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::StatusCondition>)

Which conditions caused the current cluster state.
Deprecated. Use field error instead.

=item * C<< $msg->nodepool_conditions() >> / C<< $msg->nodepool_conditions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::StatusCondition>)

Which conditions caused the current node pool state.
Deprecated. Use field error instead.

=item * C<< $msg->error() >> / C<< $msg->error($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Rpc::Status::Status>)

The error result of the operation in case of failure.

=back

=head3 Enum: Operation::Status

=over 4

=item * C<STATUS_UNSPECIFIED> => C<0>

=item * C<PENDING> => C<1>

=item * C<RUNNING> => C<2>

=item * C<DONE> => C<3>

=item * C<ABORTING> => C<4>

=back

=head3 Enum: Operation::Type

=over 4

=item * C<TYPE_UNSPECIFIED> => C<0>

=item * C<CREATE_CLUSTER> => C<1>

=item * C<DELETE_CLUSTER> => C<2>

=item * C<UPGRADE_MASTER> => C<3>

=item * C<UPGRADE_NODES> => C<4>

=item * C<REPAIR_CLUSTER> => C<5>

=item * C<UPDATE_CLUSTER> => C<6>

=item * C<CREATE_NODE_POOL> => C<7>

=item * C<DELETE_NODE_POOL> => C<8>

=item * C<SET_NODE_POOL_MANAGEMENT> => C<9>

=item * C<AUTO_REPAIR_NODES> => C<10>

=item * C<AUTO_UPGRADE_NODES> => C<11>

=item * C<SET_LABELS> => C<12>

=item * C<SET_MASTER_AUTH> => C<13>

=item * C<SET_NODE_POOL_SIZE> => C<14>

=item * C<SET_NETWORK_POLICY> => C<15>

=item * C<SET_MAINTENANCE_POLICY> => C<16>

=item * C<RESIZE_CLUSTER> => C<18>

=item * C<FLEET_FEATURE_UPGRADE> => C<19>

=back

