=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool

NodePool contains the name and configuration for a cluster's node pool.
Node pools are a set of nodes (i.e. VM's), with a common configuration and
specification, under the control of the cluster master. They may have a set
of Kubernetes labels applied to them, which may be used to reference them
during pod scheduling. They may also be resized up or down, to accommodate
the workload.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->config() >> / C<< $msg->config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodeConfig>)

The node configuration of the pool.

=item * C<< $msg->initial_node_count() >> / C<< $msg->initial_node_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

The initial node count for the pool. You must ensure that your
Compute Engine [resource
quota](https://cloud.google.com/compute/quotas)
is sufficient for this number of instances. You must also have available
firewall and routes quota.

=item * C<< $msg->locations() >> / C<< $msg->locations($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The list of Google Compute Engine
[zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the NodePool's nodes should be located.

If this value is unspecified during node pool creation, the
[Cluster.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters#Cluster.FIELDS.locations)
value will be used, instead.

Warning: changing node pool locations will result in nodes being added
and/or removed.

=item * C<< $msg->network_config() >> / C<< $msg->network_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodeNetworkConfig>)

Networking configuration for this NodePool. If specified, it overrides the
cluster-level defaults.

=item * C<< $msg->self_link() >> / C<< $msg->self_link($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Server-defined URL for the resource.

=item * C<< $msg->version() >> / C<< $msg->version($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The version of Kubernetes running on this NodePool's nodes. If unspecified,
it defaults as described
[here](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/versioning#specifying_node_version).

=item * C<< $msg->instance_group_urls() >> / C<< $msg->instance_group_urls($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The resource URLs of the [managed instance
groups](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instance-groups/creating-groups-of-managed-instances)
associated with this node pool.
During the node pool blue-green upgrade operation, the URLs contain both
blue and green resources.

=item * C<< $msg->status() >> / C<< $msg->status($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1::NodePool::Status>)

Output only. The status of the nodes in this pool instance.

=item * C<< $msg->status_message() >> / C<< $msg->status_message($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Deprecated. Use conditions instead.
Additional information about the current status of this
node pool instance, if available.

=item * C<< $msg->autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePoolAutoscaling>)

Autoscaler configuration for this NodePool. Autoscaler is enabled
only if a valid configuration is present.

=item * C<< $msg->management() >> / C<< $msg->management($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodeManagement>)

NodeManagement configuration for this NodePool.

=item * C<< $msg->max_pods_constraint() >> / C<< $msg->max_pods_constraint($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::MaxPodsConstraint>)

The constraint on the maximum number of pods that can be run
simultaneously on a node in the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->conditions() >> / C<< $msg->conditions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::StatusCondition>)

Output only. Which conditions caused the current node pool state.

=item * C<< $msg->pod_ipv4_cidr_size() >> / C<< $msg->pod_ipv4_cidr_size($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Output only. The pod CIDR block size per node in this node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->upgrade_settings() >> / C<< $msg->upgrade_settings($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::UpgradeSettings>)

Upgrade settings control disruption and speed of the upgrade.

=item * C<< $msg->placement_policy() >> / C<< $msg->placement_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::PlacementPolicy>)

Specifies the node placement policy.

=item * C<< $msg->update_info() >> / C<< $msg->update_info($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::UpdateInfo>)

Output only. Update info contains relevant information during a node
pool update.

=item * C<< $msg->etag() >> / C<< $msg->etag($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of
node pool fields, and may be sent on update requests to ensure the client
has an up-to-date value before proceeding.

=item * C<< $msg->queued_provisioning() >> / C<< $msg->queued_provisioning($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::QueuedProvisioning>)

Specifies the configuration of queued provisioning.

=item * C<< $msg->best_effort_provisioning() >> / C<< $msg->best_effort_provisioning($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::BestEffortProvisioning>)

Enable best effort provisioning for nodes

=item * C<< $msg->node_drain_config() >> / C<< $msg->node_drain_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::NodeDrainConfig>)

Specifies the node drain configuration for this node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->maintenance_policy() >> / C<< $msg->maintenance_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::NodePoolMaintenancePolicy>)

Optional. Specifies the maintenance policy for the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->kubelet_cert_info() >> / C<< $msg->kubelet_cert_info($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodePool::KubeletCertInfo>)

