=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::NodeManagement

NodeManagement defines the set of node management services turned on for the
node pool.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->auto_upgrade() >> / C<< $msg->auto_upgrade($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

A flag that specifies whether node auto-upgrade is enabled for the node
pool. If enabled, node auto-upgrade helps keep the nodes in your node pool
up to date with the latest release version of Kubernetes.

=item * C<< $msg->auto_repair() >> / C<< $msg->auto_repair($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

A flag that specifies whether the node auto-repair is enabled for the node
pool. If enabled, the nodes in this node pool will be monitored and, if
they fail health checks too many times, an automatic repair action will be
triggered.

=item * C<< $msg->upgrade_options() >> / C<< $msg->upgrade_options($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::AutoUpgradeOptions>)

Specifies the Auto Upgrade knobs for the node pool.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::BestEffortProvisioning

Best effort provisioning.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->enabled() >> / C<< $msg->enabled($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

When this is enabled, cluster/node pool creations will ignore non-fatal
errors like stockout to best provision as many nodes as possible right now
and eventually bring up all target number of nodes

=item * C<< $msg->min_provision_nodes() >> / C<< $msg->min_provision_nodes($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Minimum number of nodes to be provisioned to be considered as succeeded,
and the rest of nodes will be provisioned gradually and eventually when
stockout issue has been resolved.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::AutoUpgradeOptions

AutoUpgradeOptions defines the set of options for the user to control how
