vulnerability that affects > 1 resource type.

=item * C<< $msg->bulletin_id() >> / C<< $msg->bulletin_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The ID of the bulletin corresponding to the vulnerability.

=item * C<< $msg->cve_ids() >> / C<< $msg->cve_ids($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The CVEs associated with this bulletin.

=item * C<< $msg->severity() >> / C<< $msg->severity($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The severity of this bulletin as it relates to GKE.

=item * C<< $msg->bulletin_uri() >> / C<< $msg->bulletin_uri($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The URI link to the bulletin on the website for more information.

=item * C<< $msg->brief_description() >> / C<< $msg->brief_description($value) >>

Type: C<String>

A brief description of the bulletin. See the bulletin pointed to by the
bulletin_uri field for an expanded description.

=item * C<< $msg->affected_supported_minors() >> / C<< $msg->affected_supported_minors($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The GKE minor versions affected by this vulnerability.

=item * C<< $msg->patched_versions() >> / C<< $msg->patched_versions($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The GKE versions where this vulnerability is patched.

=item * C<< $msg->suggested_upgrade_target() >> / C<< $msg->suggested_upgrade_target($value) >>

Type: C<String>

This represents a version selected from the patched_versions field that
the cluster receiving this notification should most likely want to upgrade
to based on its current version. Note that if this notification is being
received by a given cluster, it means that this version is currently
available as an upgrade target in that cluster's location.

=item * C<< $msg->manual_steps_required() >> / C<< $msg->manual_steps_required($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

If this field is specified, it means there are manual steps that the user
must take to make their clusters safe.

=item * C<< $msg->mitigated_versions() >> / C<< $msg->mitigated_versions($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The GKE versions where this vulnerability is mitigated.

=back

