=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::LocalNvmeSsdBlockConfig

LocalNvmeSsdBlockConfig contains configuration for using raw-block local
NVMe SSDs

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->local_ssd_count() >> / C<< $msg->local_ssd_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Number of local NVMe SSDs to use.  The limit for this value is dependent
upon the maximum number of disk available on a machine per zone. See:
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/local-ssd
for more information.

A zero (or unset) value has different meanings depending on machine type
being used:
1. For pre-Gen3 machines, which support flexible numbers of local ssds,
zero (or unset) means to disable using local SSDs as ephemeral storage.
2. For Gen3 machines which dictate a specific number of local ssds, zero
(or unset) means to use the default number of local ssds that goes with
that machine type. For example, for a c3-standard-8-lssd machine, 2 local
ssds would be provisioned. For c3-standard-8 (which doesn't support local
ssds), 0 will be provisioned. See
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/local-ssd#choose_number_local_ssds
for more info.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::DiskIoScheduler

DiskIoScheduler contains the configuration for the disk IO scheduler.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->node_system_io_scheduler() >> / C<< $msg->node_system_io_scheduler($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Optional. Configures the IO scheduler for the boot disk or ephemeral lssd
that runs node system workloads. Supported values are `mq-deadline`, `bfq`,
`kyber`, `none`.

=item * C<< $msg->node_attached_disk_io_scheduler() >> / C<< $msg->node_attached_disk_io_scheduler($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Optional. Configures the IO scheduler for the attached disks.
Supported values are `mq-deadline`, `bfq`, `kyber`, `none`.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::EphemeralStorageLocalSsdConfig

EphemeralStorageLocalSsdConfig contains configuration for the node ephemeral
storage using Local SSDs.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->local_ssd_count() >> / C<< $msg->local_ssd_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Number of local SSDs to use to back ephemeral storage. Uses NVMe
interfaces.

A zero (or unset) value has different meanings depending on machine type
being used:
1. For pre-Gen3 machines, which support flexible numbers of local ssds,
zero (or unset) means to disable using local SSDs as ephemeral storage. The
limit for this value is dependent upon the maximum number of disk
available on a machine per zone. See:
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/local-ssd
for more information.
2. For Gen3 machines which dictate a specific number of local ssds, zero
(or unset) means to use the default number of local ssds that goes with
that machine type. For example, for a c3-standard-8-lssd machine, 2 local
ssds would be provisioned. For c3-standard-8 (which doesn't support local
ssds), 0 will be provisioned. See
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/local-ssd#choose_number_local_ssds
for more info.

=item * C<< $msg->data_cache_count() >> / C<< $msg->data_cache_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Number of local SSDs to use for GKE Data Cache.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::ResourceManagerTags

A map of resource manager tag keys and values to be attached to the nodes
for managing Compute Engine firewalls using Network Firewall Policies.
Tags must be according to specifications in
https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/tags-firewalls-overview#specifications.
A maximum of 5 tag key-value pairs can be specified.
Existing tags will be replaced with new values.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->tags() >> / C<< $msg->tags($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1::ClusterService::ResourceManagerTags::TagsEntry>)

TagKeyValue must be in one of the following formats ([KEY]=[VALUE])
1. `tagKeys/{tag_key_id}=tagValues/{tag_value_id}`
2. `{org_id}/{tag_key_name}={tag_value_name}`
3. `{project_id}/{tag_key_name}={tag_value_name}`

=back

